---
import Layout from '../../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Muse Glimmer — Meta — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="Meta’s 30B open-weight multimodal model, distilled from Muse Spark. Apache 2.0."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Meta · Muse</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Muse Glimmer</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Muse Glimmer is Meta’s 30-billion-parameter open-weight multimodal model, distilled from Muse Spark and aimed at local agent workflows. Weights are under Apache License 2.0.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Dense, decoder-only multimodal transformer with a built-in vision encoder. Trained from Muse Spark’s outputs rather than from scratch (Meta docs). Full dataset mix and FLOPs are not published on the docs cited here.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Text and image in, text out. Default context is 128K tokens; longer contexts are supported per docs. Runs locally via vLLM, SGLang, llama.cpp, and ExecuTorch; partner hosts listed on docs include Ollama, LM Studio, and Together. No API key is required for self-host.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>Default context is 128K tokens. Exact maximum is on the live Glimmer docs.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Step-by-step reasoning before answer (docs). Distilled from Spark. Prompting and chat template: Meta Glimmer prompting guide. This is weights you run, not a chat-API SKU on the Meta Model API in the same way as Spark.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>A public third-party score table for Glimmer is not on the pages cited here. Prefer Meta research blog or docs if they publish dated evals later.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>Quantized GGUF builds are aimed at a single ~24–32 GB GPU envelope (Meta Glimmer blog / quantization docs). Exact training cluster size is not published.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Access</h2>
    <p>Hugging Face: <code>meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B</code> (bf16), <code>meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B-GGUF</code>, plus ExecuTorch / draft checkpoints per get-the-model docs. Apache 2.0.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://ai.developer.meta.com/docs/muse-glimmer">Muse Glimmer docs</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://ai.developer.meta.com/docs/muse-glimmer/get-the-model">Get the model</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://developer.meta.com/ai/resources/blog/build-with-muse-glimmer/">Build with Muse Glimmer</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
